## 🚀 Final Summary

Designing good data architecture requires more than technical knowledge. It requires understanding the business, evaluating trade-offs, anticipating failures, choosing appropriate technologies, controlling costs, protecting information, and enabling teams to work effectively.

A strong data engineer should understand not only how to build a pipeline, but also why it exists, how it fits into the wider system, how it can fail, how it can scale, and how it can evolve.

**The ultimate goal is not to build the most complicated architecture. It is to build an architecture that reliably delivers the right data, to the right people, at the right time, at an appropriate cost.**

